    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Every day, Robert Ménard, the mayor of the small French town of Béziers, sees dog poop. On the sidewalk. On the streets. All this "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "eyesore",
            "zh": "碍眼的东西"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "ruins",
            "ref": "v-ruin"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the beautiful town centre. When he catches dog owners "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "leave"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " droppings, he "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scolds",
            "ref": "v-scold"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " them. Other times, he picks them up "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now the mayor is turning up the heat by introducing a new rule. According to this rule, pet dogs must "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "have"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their DNA on file with the local government. They will each get a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "genetic",
            "zh": "基因的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " “passport” to prove this. People must carry these passports when walking their dogs in certain central parts of the town. They will be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fined",
            "ref": "v-fine"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " if they don’t do this. And if dog poop "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "find"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in public places, the town will test it to uncover which dog did it. And the owner will have to pay "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the cleanup."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The mayor hopes the new rule will help reduce "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sanitation workers’ workloads",
            "zh": "环卫工人的工作量"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5a",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5b"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5c"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", cut down on government spending. Every year, the town spends 80,000 euros ($89,495) on picking up dog poop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But how will the government make sure that the rule is carried out properly? Questions remain. The town plans "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "hire"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a lab to test the dogs’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "samples",
            "ref": "v-sample"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But how "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "accurate",
            "ref": "v-accurate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " will the DNA test results be? And how much are they going to cost? It isn’t sure yet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Dog "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "feces",
            "zh": "排泄物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " left on streets can be a risk to public health. They may carry "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bacteria",
            "ref": "v-bacteria"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that can spread to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " animals and to people. Sometimes this may cause disease."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The city will "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "organisation"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " free DNA tests for dogs. Owners can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "submit",
            "ref": "v-submit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their dogs’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "saliva",
            "zh": "口水"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " samples and receive their dogs’ passports. Dog owners can also go to their vets for the service."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The rule mostly applies to locals. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a visitor to Béziers doesn’t pick up his dog’s droppings, “I’m not going to bother him,” said the mayor. In fact, outsiders aren’t the problem, he said. “It’s us, the people of Béziers, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " don’t do the work. We are the ones who must lead by example,” he added."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
